@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "okta.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki to Okta Employee Integration
	Testing employee sync updates in koroneiki caused by changes in okta.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View Liferay employee on Account Access EU group
	New Liferay employees who are added to koroneiki via okta in the Employees and Account Access EU groups should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | okt.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OKT                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	| Group         | Account Access EU                |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	And the support user with the email address "okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer"
	And the support user with the email address "okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - DXP"
	And the support user with the email address "okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Portal"
	And the support user with the email address "okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Commerce"
	And the user with the email address "okt.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Account Access EU"

